Descriptive statistics aim to summarise the characteristics of data, thereby facilitating the understanding of trends and variations within the dataset. They also serve as an initial stage of data screening before further statistical analyses are conducted. In the scale of this study, descriptive statistics include the minimum, maximum, mean, and standard deviation (SD) scores. The correlation values assume that the data are normally distributed and exhibit a linear relationship. The correlation coefficient ($r
